{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 54, :comments ["<b>To the Tent of Meeting, a memorial, etc., before HaShem.</b> One needs to know why the verse wrote in this order, that it interposed between the mention of the place and the phrase ״לִפְנֵי ה׳״ — for it should have said ״אֶל אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד לִפְנֵי ה׳ זִכָּרוֹן לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״? And the verse is explained in light of what they said in tractate Kallah, and this is their language: Rav Achai bar Yoshiah said, whoever distances himself from transgression — even if he is an ordinary Israelite — he is worthy to offer an olah-offering like a High Priest upon the altar, etc., end of quote. And in our case, all the articles of handiwork that the officers had taken came from the men who had distanced themselves from transgression, and the vessels came from the very substance of the matter, for they — may their memory be for blessing (Song of Songs 6:6) — had such been their practice in that war: when they would strip the women of their ornaments, they would smear their own faces with mud and mire, and they would pull the nose-rings off them so as not to gaze upon them. And this is what was intended by the verse's attaching the phrase ״לִפְנֵי ה׳״ to the phrase ״לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״ — for these Israelites are worthy to be לִפְנֵי ה׳ according to the statement of Rav Achai bar Yoshiah, and the matter would serve as a memorial."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:16:23.259369743Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}